a-Fig/Accordion, revision d34b5d09ebe9e06e8279516d169e773bed4b05da, branch devmain,
  version 0.1.2 (2026-09-29). Re-ported 2026-10-01 from 84271452ebd3650d0f63fbf77810693299b19ea9
  (branch main, 2026-09-16), 26 commits on. Note the branch: upstream's main was, and still is,
  the older revision the first vendoring took, so a re-read of main shows nothing new.
  Covers: pi-packages/accordion/ — extension/, core/, conductors/, and the single
  shared module app/src/lib/live/registry.ts that the extension imports.
  Not copied from upstream: app/ (the SvelteKit + Tauri desktop app) except that one
  module, brand/, docs/, .github/, and accordion.js. Upstream does not commit
  accordion.js either; it is built at prepack for the npm tarball, which is why the
  vendored copy points pi at extension/accordion.ts instead.
  COMMITTED GENERATED OUTPUT: extension/dist/client/, the browser build behind the
  Map. Upstream ships it in the npm package and never commits it to git; it is
  committed here because it cannot be rebuilt from this tree, the client build
  needing app/.
  LOCAL DELTAS, FIVE of them, all listed in Packs/harness/README.md and all reversible
  without touching upstream's structure. Two are behavioural, inside
  extension/accordion.ts and both env-reversible rather than literal flips: folding is
  armed from ACCORDION_FOLDING_DEFAULT and a catalog-validated conductor attached from
  ACCORDION_CONDUCTOR_DEFAULT, where upstream hardcodes setFolding(false); and native
  compaction is cancelled only while a conductor is attached, where upstream cancels it
  whenever folding is armed. Two are packaging: this Pack's root package.json points pi
  at extension/accordion.ts, and that same wrapper adds the vitest runner the upstream
  suite was written for. The fifth moves the attention probe's CUDA build from 12.1 to
  12.6.
  WRAPPER DELTA, outside the vendored trees: the root package.json beside them adds
  a pinned devDependency on vitest and a `test` script, so the upstream suite runs
  under the runner it was written for. Every *.test.ts under this directory is
  upstream's, byte-identical and vendored as-is; upstream's runner is vitest, and
  Bun's `vi` shim does not implement advanceTimersByTimeAsync, so `bun test` reported
  seven failures in code Axon did not write. bunfig.toml scopes `bun test` away from
  Packs/*/pi-packages/**, and the CI bun-tests job runs `bun run test` inside this
  directory instead (24 files, 552 tests, green from 2026-10-01). The tests are kept
  rather than dropped because they carry upstream's coverage of the two conductors and
  the signed-thinking flag this re-port brought in. They are NOT coverage of the two
  behavioural deltas above, and saying otherwise was measured false: reverting either
  one in turn on 2026-10-01 leaves the suite passing 552/552 while extension/smoke.mjs
  fails, which is why CI runs smoke as its own step.
  https://github.com/a-Fig/Accordion
